{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has","id":1448404,"title":"[Revised] In your idea of Caine,which disciplines does he has?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-13T04:08:56-07:00","id":1448404,"title":"[Revised] In your idea of Caine,which disciplines does he has?","content":"according to the description of the Path of Caine,both in Chaining thr Beast and Guide to the Sabbat. It is said Caine didn't have the more complext disciplines,like Serpentis and Obeah. And that the Path is only not opposed to Vicissitude and Obtenebration because those are very common on the Sabbat.<br /> which makes me wonder. In your idea of Caine,if you have one, does he truly has no other disciplines other than the basic ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T05:02:01-07:00","id":1448406,"title":"","content":"I disagree with the Path of Caine. They have no first hand knowledge of what Caine can and can\u2019t do. I think Caine has access to every discipline except Thaumaturgy, including Oblivion (no reason Caine can\u2019t control the Abyss) and non-Tremere blood magic paths (a lot of other clans besides the Tremere developed blood magic and I think Caine as the father of vampires has access to any form of blood magic practiced by his descendants, which the Tremere aren\u2019t since they were originally mages who transformed themselves into vampires). Also I don\u2019t think Vicissitude is a disease like it says in the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra guide. I think it\u2019s a regular discipline created by the clan founder like any other discipline.<br /> <br /> Did you know that Vicissitude literally means a crisis or a problem? Like an obstacle in life?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> do you guys have any opinion on this issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-13-2021, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T05:26:03-07:00","id":1448408,"title":"","content":"It's not even certain that Caine exists as a person, so any claims about his disciplines are just speculation. For all we know, Caine is simply the platonic embodiment of murder, and not even a vampire, merely the creator of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T05:46:47-07:00","id":1448411,"title":"","content":"Considering Caine learned the discipline from Lilith, and 5th edition reduced the number of disciplines.<br /> It it safe to assume that it has them all.<br /> Blood Magic existed before Tremere, and who would be better adept of blood magic than Lilith, called the first witch by some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25881-mr-stick","name":"Mr. Stick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T07:37:25-07:00","id":1448419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Stick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1448411#post1448411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Caine learned the discipline from Lilith, and 5th edition reduced the number of disciplines.<br /> It it safe to assume that it has them all.<br /> Blood Magic existed before Tremere, and who would be better adept of blood magic than Lilith, called the first witch by some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! I totally agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T09:38:43-07:00","id":1448430,"title":"","content":"I don't believe that Caine has any Disciplines as we know them, rather he has a single unfettered ur-Discipline akin to blood magic. As in, he can mimic or create (or cancel!) any effect he wishes and is not restrained by the whole &quot;Discipline level&quot; idea (which I also believe is a side effect of the Curse of Generation). So Caine wouldn't actually need Auspex 9 to enact False Slumber, he just takes a torpor nap and takes an astral walkabout naturally. Just like he probably doesn't have Celerity, he just thinks &quot;I want to go fast,&quot; and it happens, or that he believes the Curse of the Sevenfold Wrath makes him physically more resilient rather than possessing Fortitude, because God smiting every thorn that scratched him, every gnat that bit him, or every jackass New York pedestrian that bumped him would be a full time job for a whole cohort of angels.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T12:23:32-07:00","id":1448450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1448408#post1448408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not even certain that Caine exists as a person, so any claims about his disciplines are just speculation. For all we know, Caine is simply the platonic embodiment of murder, and not even a vampire, merely the creator of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this take. I think Caine should be a mysterious figure, and while NPCs in the setting can have firm beliefs about the exact nature of Caine, I don't think it means anyone has any real evidence as to what his real status is. It's all speculation based on whatever assumptions that character has (which at this point is likely entirely based on someone else's speculations disguised as concrete evidence which in turn was also based on someone's speculations long past). Followers of the Path of Caine are vampires who follow a semi-religious orthodox line concerning the figure of Caine, and aren't actually trying to learn the truth, just new bits they can force into a pre-conceived notion of Caine.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, &quot;Caine&quot; is a placeholder name given for the progenitor of vampires. But that doesn't necessarily mean Caine himself was a vampire, or even the Biblical figure of Cain. He might have been some kind of wizard who discovered a dark secret source of power that was used on or by others (the second generation). Or some sort of strange creature that still wasn't what we would call a vampire now. It's entirely possible that prior to the Deluge, nobody was truly a &quot;vampire&quot;. But the antedeluvians who survived were transformed as a result of changes to the world that occurred as a result of the Deluge, and thus the first vampires as we recognize them today. (not to mention what the Deluge might actually have been.)<br /> <br /> I think all too often STs and game developers take a far too pedestrian approach to the concepts of Caine, the Deluge, and the antedeluvian world. Not only does it lack the grandeur of the apocryphal Book of Enoch, it lacks the creativity, majesty, and dark wonder of similar concepts like Marvel Comics origin of vampires with Varnae and the Darkhold cult in Atlantis, or Mike Mignola's Helboy's mythos with the Black Goddess, Hyperborea, the Ogdru Jahad, and the Cold People.<br /> <br /> I would never use Caine as an actual character in my chronicles as it would reduce the mystery. But I do have concepts, artifacts, and lore about him and the antedeluvian world which PC Noddist scholars can encounter. Real Noddist scholars in my chronicles (primarily NPCs, as I find few PCs are truly interested in these kind of things that have little practical value) usually find enough information that causes them to greatly challenge the standard Noddist myth known in the books and held by the Sabbat. Some retreat into the certainties of the legend that has been constructed and just become a hack. Those brave enough to carry on in true scholarship quickly realize they are heretics, but keep quiet lest they be destroyed by the Sabbat for their heretical/blasphemous views. Only some of the Gehenna Cults and a few independent scholars in the Camarilla are able to explore their ideas with relative freedom.<br /> <br /> In short, questions like what kind of Disciplines did Caine have or does have, is not only unimportant, it's probably one of the least interesting questions to ask from a gaming perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T17:19:41-07:00","id":1448478,"title":"","content":"In my interpretation, Caine isn't really a vampire or even undead. He's just a proto human (meaning more innately powerful) who was cursed with absolute immortality by god, and then awakened in the manner of a mage by Lilith's blood magicks. He doesn't have disciplines, just raw power directed with will and fueled by his vitae. Disciplines are just a pale imitation of the kind of unfettered power that Caine has, just as Caine's childer are just pale imitations of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T17:47:22-07:00","id":1448482,"title":"","content":"Caine (or whatever his original name was) is for all intents and purposes a godlike being and a plot device who can do whatever he(?) needs to be able to do for the story. At least that's how I'd treat him if I ever used him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T18:05:17-07:00","id":1448484,"title":"","content":"Caine has all the Disciplines. All of them.<br /> <br /> I justify this by assuming that, as the progenitor of all vampires, he can &quot;read&quot; the blood of his every descendant. Every (Cainite) vampire that exists, ever existed, and will ever exist descends from Caine, and thus by the Principle of Contagion, he can draw upon the potency of their blood and gain access to their powers.<br /> <br /> The moment any (Cainite) vampire, anywhere, invents a new Discipline power, Caine either knows about it or will learn about it promptly. He learns about it, shrugs his shoulders, and begins thinking of ways he can iterate upon it in ways no lesser vampire could ever accomplish (both because of insufficiently potent blood and from lack of experience with using Disciplines in general). It's my headcanon that Caine learned the Path of Blood long ago, and by now has enhanced it to the point where he need not bother feeding manually. He simply siphons particles of blood from people's bodies in minute quantities, so small they don't notice the absence, and can do so to entire crowds of people at the same time. That is how Caine feeds. He just walks through a crowd of people, and comes out the other end completely topped off.<br /> <br /> It's my contention that Caine not only has all the Disciplines, he has all of them at 10 dots. Caine has Plot Device level powers in every Discipline. This is why any rendering of his statline reads &quot;You Lose&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T18:21:05-07:00","id":1448486,"title":"","content":"I mean I guess it just depends on what you envision him as doing. If he's just been sleeping in topor for thousands of years then there's probably a lot of Disciplines he doesn't know. On the other hand if you decide he's been spending his unlife disguised as a neonate, joining various factions and then leaving, all in a search for a way to break his curse, he might have nearly any of the Disciplines. And, of course, you could always do something like Bluecho and give him a magical way to know everything. <br /> <br /> Cain's never appeared in my games (in some of them I figure he's just a literal myth and doesn't even exist), so what Disciplines he may or may not have has never come up for me. I'd probably give him all of the traditional Disciplines at very high levels, but more obscure or unique ones like Nihilistics or Obeh he probably wouldn't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T13:14:54-07:00","id":1448532,"title":"","content":"So third gens go to 10<br /> Do second gens go to 11?<br /> Does Caine go to 12?<br /> Perhaps Caine's just a really, really, really strong mage with a lot of paradox on him, and the second generation are his experiments/disciplines who went on to replicate his experiments. Going into settite mode; Perhaps he's an emanation, a being from outside of reality that has entered it to provide those trapped within a way out; Vitae is his alchemy.<br /> <br /> Fo reals, I kinda like that one joke Caine Character sheet where his stats are &quot;YOU LOSE&quot;. If we go with less speculative ideas and instead go for a more Noddist approach, then he has neither Obtenebration nor Vicissitude. What he does have, are the common disciplines, every conceivable thaumaturgical path, and a kind of 'ultimate Protean' which is basically whatever he wants; Serpentis, Thanatosis, Visceraticka? All are within the confines of his ultimate Protean.<br /> <br /> The things I'm on the fence about are Necromancy, Chimestry, and if he'd have some kind of Diamonion/Valeren/Spiritus power. Necromancy's Degenerate and I don't see him as the type to want to learn Ash or Bones, but he's so old he probably would've learned sephulcre for convenience. Chimestry's that power that you kinda think more vampires should have, and it's not got the same baggage as Viscissitude/Obtenebration. Lastly, the dude supposedly defied angels, shouldn't he have some kind of.. spirit based Discipline like Diamonion or Valeren? Or perhaps his experience makes him stand against such things, which is why saulot is such a heretic for trying them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T18:28:11-07:00","id":1448554,"title":"","content":"In my wildest version of head-canon, Caine was the First Marauder. His botched Awakening drove him to madness and the Sundering was the creation of the first Marauder reality bubble in which, because it started so early in pre-history, the entire world finds itself inside (including the entire paradigm of the modern world where Caine's immortal descendants have always existed... even the attempts to reframe him as a myth still operate within the paradigm of his reality bubble... that immortal vampires are real).<br /> <br /> Inside the reality bubble he IS the child of the First Mortals and was cursed by the angels (actually just how his Avatar manifests) and inside that warped reality he passed his curse onto others and made them vampires. This is why Cainite history doesn't align with the broader spirit history of the Fera or Wan Kuei or Changelings; they still remember what the real history is outside Caine's bubble of madness was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T08:27:43-07:00","id":1448588,"title":"","content":"Anything and everything, including things no one has thought of. He is a walking global apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T10:13:29-07:00","id":1448703,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to come up with an idea for the evolution of Disciplines. Using as many resources as I have read, including many that I no longer own, my best guess is that Caine would have all Disciplines mentioned in the Book of Nod, as well as those Disciplines that developed from them. This would mean Caine could have, for V20 rules, Dementation, Quietus, and Sepentis. He could also have most, if not all, forms of Blood Magic, including Necromancy. He would not have Chimerstry, which I feel was stolen from the Fae; Obtenebration, which is from the Abyss; and Vicissitude, which might come from either the Deep Umbra or the Underworld. He could also have bloodline Disciplines descended from the clan sets, but not those evolved from non-clan Disciplines. He could easily learn most, if not all, of these extra Disciplines, as he is not bound by in-Clan/bloodline costs. He is unbound by generation, so he could master any such new Discipline fairly quickly, as well as develop new individual powers for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T05:42:58-07:00","id":1448846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1448554#post1448554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my wildest version of head-canon, Caine was the First Marauder. His botched Awakening drove him to madness and the Sundering was the creation of the first Marauder reality bubble in which, because it started so early in pre-history, the entire world finds itself inside (including the entire paradigm of the modern world where Caine's immortal descendants have always existed... even the attempts to reframe him as a myth still operate within the paradigm of his reality bubble... that immortal vampires are real).<br /> <br /> Inside the reality bubble he IS the child of the First Mortals and was cursed by the angels (actually just how his Avatar manifests) and inside that warped reality he passed his curse onto others and made them vampires. This is why Cainite history doesn't align with the broader spirit history of the Fera or Wan Kuei or Changelings; they still remember what the real history is outside Caine's bubble of madness was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T09:06:08-07:00","id":1448872,"title":"","content":"I think context matters. In this case especially the answer will differ depending on that context. Like Doylist/Watsonian views. <br /> <br /> In a pure mechanical view (Doylist) you have Caine being 'super plot device' powerful so he basically has whatever he needs to do what he needs when he needs. It's entirely up to the storyteller. The hows and whys might matter for story purposes, or they might not. For story purposes Caine might not even exist (as some pointed out.) <br /> <br /> Narrative view (Watsonian) it gets more complicated. If you assume the legends have some truth to them and Caine exists, it gets a bit more interesting. One of the things I always remember is how much WW mythology loves cycles. What goes around, comes around. And with the way the vampiric curse works... you have the ancients who created many of the modern disciplines (including the Clan specific ones)... then you have the caitiff (and/or ultimately thin bloods) who have some measure of that same power themselves despite their 'weaker' blood. Logically it follows that if you loop around from Thin Bloods you get to... well, Caine. The ultimate innovator (which reflects his 'Even more Deus Ex Machina' approach to disciplines than Antediluvians do.)<br /> <br /> Some sources (like Blood Magic) draw parallels between blood magic and what Caine was purported to do (this may have just been a Tremere conceit though) and in a sense you can also see Caine as the ultimate Blood Magician, albeit in a more instinctive way (Lilith would have been the more skilled, powerful one.) As MyWifeisScary suggested Caine's powers (which derive in part from Lilith's teachings) can in a sense be considered a mage (although I envisioned it working for vampires more like Requiem's Theban Sorcery or Cruac) although one can argue the ability for Caitiff, very old and very young vampires to create their own disciplines is itself akin to what mages do (again Tremere parallels come to mind.) And Lilith's ties to Awakend magic lend that some credence too I think, although Caine wouldn't incorporate it nearly the same way (in a sense he used what Lilith taught to create cruder more 'linear' approaches and down the generations and years it calcified into what became known as Disciplines.) If you borrow from 5th 'Thin Blood Alchemy' could be seen as a very weak, debaesd form of Cain's 'original' ability too much like Thaumaturgy is. <br /> <br /> I've also believed that 'Thin Blood Syndrome' (to borrow Netchurch's term) could occur at any generation (although it becomes more frequent at higher ones) which may reflect a form of Caitiff as well. The Curse can mutate and in some it may not fully take hold no matter how ancient your sire or great their blood (There was a 6th generation Vampire in the Giovanni Chronicles who still aged once every ten years, like some Thin Blood do) Caine himself may not be 'fully' a vampire due to the unusual circumstances of his creation (but he's vampire-like enough to be treated like it in most ways) and thus likewise the 'curse' affects him differently and different rules can apply. We can also go back to 'cycles' and note that Thin Bloods circle back to Caine. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T13:19:24-07:00","id":1448893,"title":"","content":"So, I've mentioned my wildest head-canon, but the fact is that I adjust the canon to fit my current chronicle (if its even necessary), so I thought I'd bring up another version I've run with.<br /> <br /> Basically it borrows from one of the options presented in BJD where Enoch's coffin is found and opened. In the version I'm thinking of Enoch is not only inside the coffin he's actually lucid and reveals that the Antediluvians aren't nearly as powerful as they pretend to be (and that the point of the Jyhad is to hide this weakness).<br /> <br /> So I ran with that idea and that, in actuality the power level we call 4th Generation actually IS the top of the scale. Now, an Antediluvian has way more XP so more things at 8-9, but they're fundamentally just 4th Gens and the Blood is constantly thickening... every vampire should they live long enough (on the scale of millennia so not generally a play consideration) will see their blood potency reach that of the 4th Generation.<br /> <br /> And here's the trick of it... because everything 4th Gen and lower has the same potency its entirely possible that they aren't even the REAL 4th Generation... just the 4th Generation recorded from a figure calling himself Caine... who might not be the first vampire... just the first one any of the Western Kindred can trace their lineages back to. The actual first vampire (who may as well be called &quot;Caine&quot; in the same way we call our oldest Mitochondrial ancestor &quot;Eve&quot; even though they may not have even been a &quot;he&quot;) might be dozens of generations further back. The Antediluvians might actually be the 13th Generation from the actual first vampire, but are regarded as the 3rd because all records of the prior generations of vampires are just lost in pre-history.<br /> <br /> In which case; Caine whether he's the actual first or just the first recorded would be a 4th Gen with maxed out stats and an outsized legend that makes people think he's second only to God in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T16:27:08-07:00","id":1448912,"title":"","content":"I loved Caine's version by Ari Marmell's Gehenna: The Final Night, that's my first murderer.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T10:50:37-07:00","id":1449199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has#post1448404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">according to the description of the Path of Caine,both in Chaining thr Beast and Guide to the Sabbat. It is said Caine didn't have the more complext disciplines,like Serpentis and Obeah. And that the Path is only not opposed to Vicissitude and Obtenebration because those are very common on the Sabbat.<br /> which makes me wonder. In your idea of Caine,if you have one, does he truly has no other disciplines other than the basic ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcanon (and games...) Caine has all the disciplines, meaning he can do whatever any vampire can do with them, including antediluvians. Even more, Caine can deprive a vampire of the power of the blood (notable exceptions, to an extent, clanless and thin bloods). He is the source of the curse after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T16:25:53-07:00","id":1449216,"title":"","content":"In my mind he has the core 9 disciplines and blood sorcery. Most below level 10. I think level 10 is extremely rare, even if you could potentially reach it because of your generation.<br /> <br /> The first three gens are equal in potential as far as i am concerned. Weakening of the blood starts with the 4th gens. But just because the first three are equal in max potential, that doesnt mean they all reached their full potential.<br /> <br /> I figure Caine was a simple farmer in life and because of this he eventually got surpassed by the greatest of the antes. The antes were some of the greatest humans of their time. As humans they were miles ahead of Caine. It took them some time to surpass Caine as vampires (mainly because Caine had a big head start) but most of them surpassed him nonetheless. Which ones is up for debate but i think Saulot, Set, Haqim, Ennoia and Tzimisce are the ones who most likely surpassed Caine. Possible also Lasombra and Malkav.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-21-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T17:01:21-07:00","id":1449220,"title":"","content":"Caine is supposed to be 200000+ years old. I doubt any ante at 8000 years old is gonna surpass him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T11:30:58-07:00","id":1449273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449220#post1449220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine is supposed to be 200000+ years old. I doubt any ante at 8000 years old is gonna surpass him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supposed? What does that mean? Nobody knows how old any of them are. But there is also a thing called diminishing returns. No one gets indefinetely more powerful. After a certain point age is just a number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T18:15:35-07:00","id":1449297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449216#post1449216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my mind he has the core 9 disciplines and blood sorcery. Most below level 10. I think level 10 is extremely rare, even if you could potentially reach it because of your generation.<br /> <br /> The first three gens are equal in potential as far as i am concerned. Weakening of the blood starts with the 4th gens. But just because the first three are equal in max potential, that doesnt mean they all reached their full potential.<br /> <br /> I figure Caine was a simple farmer in life and because of this he eventually got surpassed by the greatest of the antes. The antes were some of the greatest humans of their time. As humans they were miles ahead of Caine. It took them some time to surpass Caine as vampires (mainly because Caine had a big head start) but most of them surpassed him nonetheless. Which ones is up for debate but i think Saulot, Set, Haqim, Ennoia and Tzimisce are the ones who most likely surpassed Caine. Possible also Lasombra and Malkav.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think Caine is a semi-divine figure who only never achieved full godhood because his cosmos was monotheistic and only allowed for one true God (the One/El/YHVH/etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T21:38:03-07:00","id":1449757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449273#post1449273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supposed? What does that mean? Nobody knows how old any of them are. But there is also a thing called diminishing returns. No one gets indefinetely more powerful. After a certain point age is just a number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by our history and Cain being one of the first humans, anatomical modern humans first appeared around 200k years ago. So he would be around that old. The 2nd gen were embraced after cities were a thing, which was around 10,000 BC. The Assamite clanbook has Haqim as one of the oldest (toreador claim Arikel is the oldest but its not wholly different in time scale), and he was embraced around 8,000 BC.<br /> <br /> If Caine is still around in the modern times, I would say he has maxed out the base disciplines and blood magic, because he went through the awakening ceremony and would know of magic. The specialty disciplines he likely would have knowledge of, but not skilled with because they are &quot;beneath him&quot;, but he has the ability to negate their effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:30:57-07:00","id":1449804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449297#post1449297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. I think Caine is a semi-divine figure who only never achieved full godhood because his cosmos was monotheistic and only allowed for one true God (the One/El/YHVH/etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it's presumably monothiestic, but it's not actually a one-god system. Look at how gnostics (including, but not limited to the Settites) view things: Careful attention should be placed to the difference between the True One-Above-All god, the hieghest god of all universes, and the Demiurge, the presumably malevolent creator of our reality, a lowly god who has made himself the biggest fish in his own pond, who has imprisoned our souls here and demands sole worship. In this vision of cosmology, Caine is a divine being sent from outside of the demiurge's creation in order to help liberate us from the prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:09:00-07:00","id":1450018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449757#post1449757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going by our history and Cain being one of the first humans, anatomical modern humans first appeared around 200k years ago. So he would be around that old. The 2nd gen were embraced after cities were a thing, which was around 10,000 BC. The Assamite clanbook has Haqim as one of the oldest (toreador claim Arikel is the oldest but its not wholly different in time scale), and he was embraced around 8,000 BC.<br /> <br /> If Caine is still around in the modern times, I would say he has maxed out the base disciplines and blood magic, because he went through the awakening ceremony and would know of magic. The specialty disciplines he likely would have knowledge of, but not skilled with because they are &quot;beneath him&quot;, but he has the ability to negate their effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we could debate about what max potential means. Maybe he has reached level 10 in most discliplines. Maybe there are levels beyond that. But my point is whatever levels of power Caine achieved, so did the antes (and then some!). Because they were inherently superior as humans and after a certain point your age doesnt matter, just your max potential.<br /> <br /> You will stop growing in power! where that point is, is ofcourse debatable! after 10,000 years? 20,000? 200,000? a miljoen? i think its around the 8-10 thousand mark. You may feel differently. So his added years (however many years they may be) wouldnt make him more powerful then the antes in my book.<br /> <br /> <br /> About your point about Caine's age:<br /> <br /> If we are going by the bible (where the myth of Caine comes from) then the world is about 6000 years old. As the first human he would be no older then that. But we know from scientific research that the first humans appeared like 200k (150k?) years ago. So you are mixing the biblical Cain with actual world history. You can't have your cake and eat it too! And who is to say he actually is the first human? Maybe thats propaganda on his part.<br /> <br /> And his ability to negate anything is pure speculation. There isnt enough information about him in the source material to say anything about his age or abilities. Its all headcanon and i place the oldest of the immortals (and that includes Caine) at 10,000 BC (give or take a few centuries). Again you may feel differently. But i cant imagine the guy spend 200,000 years wandering alone on this earth without siring anyone or that he did sire, but they all died somehow until the second gen antes came around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-28-2021, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:17:27-07:00","id":1450023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1449297#post1449297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. I think Caine is a semi-divine figure who only never achieved full godhood because his cosmos was monotheistic and only allowed for one true God (the One/El/YHVH/etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats fine. That your headcanon! But personally, i dont like the idea of bringing god or gods into the lore. Its so ridiculous to me that i cant connect with it at all. Caine might have ideas of godhood (he is probably that arrogant) but he is nowhere near the levels of cosmic beings (who may or may ot exist) as far as i am concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-28-2021, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T19:18:00-07:00","id":1450253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1450023#post1450023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thats fine. That your headcanon! But personally, i dont like the idea of bringing god or gods into the lore. Its so ridiculous to me that i cant connect with it at all. Caine might have ideas of godhood (he is probably that arrogant) but he is nowhere near the levels of cosmic beings (who may or may ot exist) as far as i am concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but if you believe Cain(e) is the Biblical Cain, then he definitely had contact with a being who claimed to be the divine creator of the world. That\u2019s not headcanon, that\u2019s from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T19:27:50-07:00","id":1450255,"title":"","content":"Related question: has anyone here actually used Caine in a game? I can recall having used him precisely once, and I just made him dispense some wisdom and used Temporis to give a player a second chance at a key decision. In other words, he displayed exactly one discipline, and used it exactly once as the plot required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T20:30:04-07:00","id":1450264,"title":"","content":"Assuming a chronicle in which Caine literally assigned each clan their signature weakness, as described in in-game legend, then he has at least one power that no other vampire appears to have figured out.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, if I were ever to run a game so unhinged that he was worth statting out, I'd assign him any discipline that isn't the sole property of a single clan. Leave room for Saulot, Hakim, Lasombra, Malkav, Ilyes, Set, Zapathasura, and the Eldest to have genuinely invented something to further their own Jyhad schemes; just give Caine the iconic vampire stuff that's firmly entrenched in pop culture - strength, fortitude, speed, hypnosis, seduction, bat form, all that Hollywood jazz. His ace in the hole is that he's the oldest and strongest and protected by a curse from God. He doesn't need a special ace in the hole beyond that, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-29-2021, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:34:53-07:00","id":1450298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1450253#post1450253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but if you believe Cain(e) is the Biblical Cain, then he definitely had contact with a being who claimed to be the divine creator of the world. That\u2019s not headcanon, that\u2019s from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ofcourse its headcanon because its not clear who wrote the Book of Nod or the Erciyes fragments. Caine seemed to have a hand in their writing. Maybe even wrote some parts of it himself. Or perhaps others wrote what he wanted. See where i am going with this? It could all be propaganda on his part. Caine is a arrogant prick , he would want the world to think that he is so important, that the almighty himself took notice of him. And beyond that, i am sure you can see the value of letting the world think you are protected by a curse from god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T04:56:59-07:00","id":1450304,"title":"","content":"I'd actually lean into the concept presented by V5 - there are eight original core disciplines, and the clans all evolved their own variants. Caine would have all original disciplines to 10 dots ramped right past personal and gothic/political horror and straight into the realm of the cosmic.<br /> <br /> However, he wouldn't neccessarily have some of them as modern kindred would recognise them. He may have blood sorcery, but blood sorcerers won't recognise anything he does with it and he wouldn't know &quot;modern&quot; paradigms either. No koldunism, no necromancy, no setite sorcery. He certainly wouldn't know thaumaturgy, because the Tremere didn't actually get embraced properly and get their practice from Caine, they invited themselves and brought their stuff with them.<br /> His own magic probably doesn't run on anything resembling logic comprehensible to a psyche on either humanity or a path of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> His shapeshifting may have some semblance to both a gangrel's protean and a tzimisce's vicissitude, but not quite be either. How does that work? Well his stats simply declare &quot;you lose&quot; and he's possibly a divine eldricht abomination from the dawn of human history, so logic doesn't necessarily matter here. I'd imagine that the primordial vampire wouldn't simply alter his human shell or shift into an animal, he would physically become a monster out of nightmares and beyond comprehension.<br /> <br /> His take on celerity is probably mashed up with temporis, so he sort of fucks up time and might exist outside of it.<br /> <br /> I actually wouldn't give him specialty stuff like Obtenebration, Valeren, Obeah or any blood magic paths.<br /> Dementation and Chimestry I'm not sure about. Part of me says yes, the other says no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-30-2021, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T09:38:46-07:00","id":1450319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1450298#post1450298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ofcourse its headcanon because its not clear who wrote the Book of Nod or the Erciyes fragments. Caine seemed to have a hand in their writing. Maybe even wrote some parts of it himself. Or perhaps others wrote what he wanted. See where i am going with this? It could all be propaganda on his part. Caine is a arrogant prick , he would want the world to think that he is so important, that the almighty himself took notice of him. And beyond that, i am sure you can see the value of letting the world think you are protected by a curse from god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but if you believe that Caine the first vampire and Cain from Genesis are the same person, then the rest of the backstory kinda falls into place.<br /> <br /> By you I mean you the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-30-2021, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T10:19:43-07:00","id":1450325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1450319#post1450319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but if you believe that Caine the first vampire and Cain from Genesis are the same person, then the rest of the backstory kinda falls into place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting on the whole Biblical Cain thing is that it was oral history long before it was ever written down. There's lots of discussion in history/sociology circles about oral histories and their accuracy, but from what I've read the consensus seems to be that oral histories tend to get broad events right, but what varies is the context assigned them.<br /> <br /> For example, we know a flood happened. There's geological evidence that the end of last Ice Age coincided with a rapid rise in sea level that would have inundated coastal communities. This also shows up in myths around the world and even coincides with the supposed date of Atlantis' destruction. Oral histories carried that event forward until it could be written down. Not knowing about the concept of cyclical ice ages, most of these stories related the event to some form of divine punishment and wrapped a morality tale around it... but the actual event; a flood that wiped out civilization as it was then known; was real.<br /> <br /> So in this context, its likely that the Cain/Abel story is actually an oral recollection of a real event in that culture's past that has similarly had a morality tale wrapped around it by later generations; basically there's no reason that Biblical Cain and &quot;Blood Caine&quot; (akin to Mitochondrial Eve) couldn't be the same person, but Biblical Cain was only written down after countless generations of oral transmission and so doesn't have everything right... just the gist of &quot;squabbled with and killed his brother then got exiled.&quot; (in WoD lore terms it obviously missed the &quot;he got turned into the first vampire).<br /> <br /> Thus, the way to read both the Book Nod, Lilith's book and the Erycie's Fragments is to take the broad strokes of EVENTS as true, but completely ignore any MOTIVATIONS assigned to any act in the text because those are most likely to have been altered to fit the author's narrative. Ex. Julius Caeser was murdered by members of the Roman Senate is the event... whether this was justified because he was a tyrant, unjustified because he was a populist aiding the common folks and killed by the elites, or just another day of politics where both sides were out for themselves and each side had both selfish and selfless motives for their actions. So I think the broad strokes of Caine is the first, he embraced several 2nd Gens and founded a city. WHY he chose to do so is more nebulous. Similarly, that it was wiped out in a flood seems likely to be real, but it may not have been a result of God's wrath, just unfortunate location relative to rising water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T10:23:45-07:00","id":1450326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448404-revised-in-your-idea-of-caine-which-disciplines-does-he-has?p=1450325#post1450325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This also shows up in myths around the world and even coincides with the supposed date of Atlantis' destruction. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Atlantis wasn't a myth. It was a professional work of fiction that was understood to be fiction when it was created.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],